well, i made it.  

no doubt many spoilers in here.  

I wonder, though, if there is anyone who DOESN'T read the spoilers.  ;)

I'd like to thank jit and lovesexy (newbie players on my local system),
whose many wizard bones piles were valuable sources of wands, rings,
and spellbooks.

Most of all, though, i'd like to thank the wand of wishing I found on
level 4; made things pretty easy (for the record, I used it for a
blessed +3 Gray dragon scale mail, the blessed rustproof +3 mjollnir, 3
blessed scrolls of charging, blessed fireproof +3 speed boots, blessed
+3 rustproof gauntlets of power, a Wand of Polymorph, and then when i
got bored polypiling I burned the last wish on a Shield of Reflection).

I found two magic lamps, which were a great light source (never run
out, natch), one of which I used for a magic marker to write some
blessed scrolls of remove curse for the endgame (again, polypiling
failed me).

I never used any wishes from the WoW from the castle, and I still had
it and one of my magic lamps when I ascended.  

this game was notable in a few ways:
 1) obviously, WoW in beginning made it easy.  Unfortunately, i almost
    bit it when i ran across a large mimic in a shop right near where
    i found the wand (but had identified it and gotten my GDSM).  Luckily
    Mojo was only a zap away; i walked away from the large mimic corpse
    with 4 hit points.  (i had a long sword already, and had planned 
    to sacrifice for a named weapon to conserve the wish)

 2) The Lady was extremely stingy until late in the game, and never did
    give me a good weapon when I sacrificed (for the record she gave me
    DragonBane (whoopie), Vorpal Blade when named Envoy of Balance, and
    Cleaver late in game when i was hoping for MagicBane).

 3) Didn't really matter though since artifacts seemed to be about a dime
    a dozen; I got Sunsword from an Archon on the Medusa level, and found
    cursed -1 Grayswandir lying on the floor in Gehemmon (definitely NOT
    a bones level).  Also found +0 Frost Brand later on in Gehemmon, and
    I noticed at least three artifact weapons in the Elemental planes 
    (Archon on fire plane had Demonbane, and Fire Brand and something 
    else were on the Astral Plane).  Tried to dip for Excalibur after I
    found a helm of opposite alignment, but got bored, and since I had 
    autosearching as a tourist, and Mojo and Vorpy by this time, I didn't
    bother after failing a few times.  

 4) Polymorphing was very good to my pets:  my original puppy Moof became
    a baluchtherium pretty early on when he stepped on a trap; this was
    kind of a drag though since he killed at least one priest before I 
    had a chance to make a donation.  He eventually died at Fort Ludios,
    I never could figure out what killed him, there was nothing strong over
    near where he was so he must just have been down on hit points.  
     Later, there was a poly trap right by the stairs on my home base
    stash level, this gave me a couple elves through the poly trick.
    The pet code needs some work, i think.  These suckers would wield
    long swords, but would not wear the perfectly good elven mithril I
    gave them, nor use the wands of magic missile i gave them, nor
    wield better weapons when given them (ie, i bought one of them a +1
    katana but he kept his +0 long sword).
     Did end up with a pet yellow mold.  that was kind of a drag, but 
    I also had a Wand of Polymorph and The Card so it was OK. 
     Another complaint with the pet code is that pets seem to be pretty
    stupid about constantly attacking even if they are low on hit
    points.

 5) polypiling gems got me my high score;        
        287 uncursed sapphires (worth 861000 zorkmids),
        135 uncursed aquamarine stones (worth 202500 zorkmids),
        186 uncursed emeralds (worth 465000 zorkmids),
        230 uncursed dilithium crystals (worth 1035000 zorkmids),
        35 uncursed turquoise stones (worth 70000 zorkmids),
        186 uncursed diamonds (worth 744000 zorkmids),
        124 uncursed rubies (worth 434000 zorkmids),
        28 uncursed amber stones (worth 28000 zorkmids)
    Clearly you can do better if you keep polypiling till you have loads
    of dilithium.  I discarded any gems that were worth less than
    1000 zorkmids (actually i tended to throw them at unicorns) since
    it's just impossible to carry that many.  I was burdened all the
    way through the endgame due to my gems (and a bucket's worth of holy
    water).  
    [r.g.h readers; this was more for the benefit of my local hack 
    mailing list; also, my score was calculated to beat our previous
    high score, which was about 7.3M ;) ]
 
 6) The Quest was remarkably easy this time around; i died at the bottom
    of the quest in my previous best Tourist game.
 
 7) the run for the surface was getting pretty annoying with the whole
    level teleport back thing, happened a lot more this time than last.  
